  "id": "COMPOUND:43828 - PROTEIN:6340",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests that the compound [(3aS,4R,9S,10aS)-2,6-diamino-10,10-dihydroxy-9-sulfooxy-3a,4,8,9-tetrahydro-1H-pyrrolo[1,2-c]purin-4-yl]methoxymethanimidate] acts as a target for multiple compounds that ultimately interact with the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This compound is directly linked to the Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP, which is a target of two different compounds—2''o-Acetylpolygalcin D and clematichinenoside H—both of which in turn target the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. The evidence indicates a potential pathway where the compound may influence the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through the modulation of its target protein, Protein-tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. The scores from the paths suggest a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, but the exact mechanism of interaction remains uncertain, as the evidence does not provide direct information on how the compound affects the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex itself. The integration of these findings highlights the compound's potential role in modulating the activity of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex through its interaction with downstream targets.",
